
listen to Syslog channels vs Read from Log file 

| Source        | Method       | Reason                              |
| ------------- | ------------ | ---------------------------         |
| auth.log      | Syslog       | Native Linux logging                |
| messages      | Syslog       | Centralized system events (syslog)  |
| secure        | Syslog       | Authentication                      |
| cron          | Syslog       | Low EPS                             |
| audit.log     | Log File     | Structured audit records            |
| Apache Access | Log File     | High-volume application log         |
| Apache Error  | Log File     | Application diagnostics             |
| Nginx Logs    | Log File     | Web server logs                     |



Permissions

Some logs cannot be read by the FortiSIEM Agent without additional permissions.

Solutions considered:

ACLs using setfacl                     sudo setfacl -m u:phoenix:r /var/log/audit/audit.log
AppArmor profile adjustments (Ubuntu)  sudo aa-complain /usr/sbin/rsyslogd  (AVC error) 


Log Rotation

Linux rotates logs.

FortiSIEM should continue reading after rotation.

Check:

logrotate configuration 




